From 9e4534dd5fdea07ff6b74755ef117a31ecc0753b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samtheruby <peasea1012@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:27:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(coreelec): no green flash or back-and-forth on refresh
 rate switches

Switching the HDMI mode with the video already on screen flashed green, and
returning to the normal rate between two videos switched the TV twice (each
switch blanks it). Mute HDMI video from just before a switch until a second
after it, asked for again once the mode is set, and go back to the normal rate
only after five seconds without a video, which the next video cancels.
---
 .../coreelec/tests/coreelec_display_test.cc   |  39 +++--
 .../starboard/rdk/shared/coreelec_display.cc  | 154 ++++++++++++++----
 .../starboard/rdk/shared/coreelec_display.h   |  22 ++-
 3 files changed, 173 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)

diff --git a/starboard/contrib/rdk/src/third_party/starboard/rdk/coreelec/tests/coreelec_display_test.cc b/starboard/contrib/rdk/src/third_party/starboard/rdk/coreelec/tests/coreelec_display_test.cc
